course: dictionary
lesson: 3502
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Fashion» is one of them. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning you need. Read the whole sentence, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «Good product design is about comfort, strength and use, and a high price can also come from brand and fashion.» Here fashion means the style that is popular at a particular time. Something can cost more just because it is the style people want right now.
explain: «Romany families had lived and travelled in painted horse-drawn wagons for many years, and caravan holidays for fun were a new fashion.» Here fashion means a popular way of doing something for a while. Caravan holidays were something new that many people enjoyed.
explain: Fashion can also be a verb. In a story, a character might fashion a tool from wood, which means they make or shape it with their hands. To check, swap in make or shape: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Fashion means the style of clothes, hair and things that is popular at a particular time.
fact: «In fashion» means popular right now, and «out of fashion» means no longer popular.
fact: «After a fashion» means not very well, and «in an orderly fashion» means in a neat, organised way.
fact: To fashion something is to make or shape it with your hands.
fact: Fashions change over time: «serious faces were also the fashion» in early portraits, when people had to keep still for a long while.
exercise: «Good product design is about comfort, strength and use, and a high price can also come from brand and fashion.» Here fashion means | *The style that is popular at a particular time | A way of walking | A kind of paint | To make or shape something with your hands
exercise: «Caravan holidays for fun were a new fashion.» What does fashion mean here? | Very old | Dangerous | *A popular way of doing something for a while | To make something with your hands
exercise: Ella says a tool can be fashioned from wood. What does fashioned mean? | Painted bright red | Sold in a shop | *Made or shaped by hand | Broken into pieces
test: Which phrase means a thing is popular right now? | After a fashion | *In fashion | Out of fashion | In an orderly fashion
test: Jayden says fashion has only one meaning. What is the best answer? | Fashion is a kind of clothes only | *A word can have several meanings, and the sentence helps you pick the right one | Every word has only one meaning, so look at the first one in the dictionary | You should skip any word with more than one meaning
exam: «Scientists are not sure if the orcas' pushing of the boats is play, a fashion in the group or something else.» What does fashion mean here? | *A popular way of behaving in the group for a while | To make or shape the boats | A type of sailing boat | Clothes worn by the orcas
